\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 1. Class\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Definition:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 A 
\f0\b class
\f1\b0  is a blueprint or template used to create objects. It defines the properties (attributes) and behaviors (methods) of an object.\

\f0\b Real-time Example:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Think of a 
\f0\b Car
\f1\b0 . "Car" is a class because it defines common properties like color, brand, and speed, and actions like start() and stop().\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 2. Attributes\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Definition:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Attributes
\f1\b0  are the variables or properties of a class that store information about an object.\

\f0\b Real-time Example:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 For a 
\f0\b Student
\f1\b0  class:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Name = Rasool\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Roll Number = 101\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Branch = CSE-AI\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Here, 
\f0\b name, roll number, and branch
\f1\b0  are attributes.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 3. Encapsulation\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Definition:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Encapsulation
\f1\b0  is the process of combining data and methods into a single class and restricting direct access to the data to protect it.\

\f0\b Real-time Example:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 An 
\f0\b ATM machine
\f1\b0  hides your bank balance. You cannot directly access or change it. You can only use options like 
\f0\b Withdraw
\f1\b0 , 
\f0\b Deposit
\f1\b0 , or 
\f0\b Check Balance
\f1\b0  after entering the correct PIN.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 4. Polymorphism\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Definition:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Polymorphism
\f1\b0  means "many forms." The same method can perform different actions depending on the object.\

\f0\b Real-time Example:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 The 
\f0\b Pay
\f1\b0  button in an online shopping app:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Pay using UPI\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Pay using Credit Card\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Pay using Net Banking\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The button is the same, but it performs different actions based on the selected payment method.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 5. Inheritance\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Definition:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Inheritance
\f1\b0  allows one class (child) to acquire the properties and methods of another class (parent), promoting code reusability.\

\f0\b Real-time Example:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 A 
\f0\b Smartphone
\f1\b0  inherits features from a 
\f0\b Phone
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Phone features: Calling, Messaging\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Smartphone adds: Camera, Internet, Apps\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The smartphone reuses the phone's features and adds new ones.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 6. Abstraction\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 Definition:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Abstraction
\f1\b0  is the process of hiding complex implementation details and showing only the essential features to the user.\

\f0\b Real-time Example:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 When you 
\f0\b drive a car
\f1\b0 , you only use the steering wheel, accelerator, brake, and gear. You don't need to know how the engine works internally. The complex details are hidden from you.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
SOME OF THE ONE LINE EXAMPLE \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Class:
\f1\b0                         Car is a class, \

\f0\b Attributes:
\f1\b0                 Car color, brand, and speed are attributes.\

\f0\b Encapsulation:
\f1\b0          ATM protects your bank balance using a PIN.\

\f0\b Polymorphism:
\f1\b0          One Pay button supports UPI, Card, and Net Banking.\

\f0\b Inheritance:
\f1\b0               Smartphone inherits calling and messaging from Phone.\

\f0\b Abstraction:             
\f1\b0  Driving a car without knowing the engine's internal working.}